WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.250
Picture an economy's control panel,

2
00:00:02.250 --> 00:00:03.970
with four dials.

3
00:00:03.970 --> 00:00:08.640
Growth. Jobs. Steady prices,
with many central banks aiming

4
00:00:08.640 --> 00:00:10.930
for about 2 per cent inflation.

5
00:00:10.930 --> 00:00:14.360
And a sustainable balance
with the rest of the world.

6
00:00:14.360 --> 00:00:17.500
Every government would love
all four needles in the green,

7
00:00:17.500 --> 00:00:19.030
at the same time.

8
00:00:19.030 --> 00:00:21.510
So why can't a government get fast growth,

9
00:00:21.510 --> 00:00:25.070
plenty of jobs and steady
prices all at once?

10
00:00:25.070 --> 00:00:28.210
In this mission, you'll weigh
growth against the environment,

11
00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.960
and against fairness.

12
00:00:29.960 --> 00:00:31.850
Then you'll use a graph lab:

13
00:00:31.850 --> 00:00:35.520
push demand harder and
watch four readouts change.

14
00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:39.120
Your mission: explain why
governments face trade-offs,

15
00:00:39.120 --> 00:00:40.670
and how they might ease them.
